LOK: a snapshot save gives way to waiting input

doc_saveAs holds the SolarMutex for the whole store, and a key takes
the same lock. Ely writes recovery points with it; a key pressed while
a large presentation was being snapshotted waited out the rest, 70 to
270 ms.
The save option Snapshot marks a copy that waiting input may stop.
comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::checkSnapshot asks the client's anyInput
callback: once before the store, then as each OOXML part's serializer
opens (sax FastSerializerHelper). A stop throws a RuntimeException;
once stopped, every later check throws too, so a filter that catches
one still ends soon. doc_saveAs then fails with "ely: stopped for
input". Saves without the option never stop.
The DOCX, XLSX and PPTX exporters now undo on any exit what they
changed on the way: Writer's redline flags, parked cursors and its
PaM ring; Calc's shortened sheet names, its external file id map and
status indicator; the drawingml graphic cache level of all three.
ODF and binary formats check only before the store starts.

